<title>BRAZIL: Brazil soybeans not hit by early frosts - Somar.</title>
<headline>Brazil soybeans not hit by early frosts - Somar.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean crops in Brazil's key growing state of Rio Grande do Sul were not affected by early frosts which affected the higher regions and the north of the state this weekend, independent meteorologist Somar said.</p>
<p>&quot;The frosts were only in the high regions,&quot; said forecaster Marcio Custodio. &quot;It didn't affect soybeans but it did hit some vegetables.&quot;</p>
<p>In Argentina, temperatures were negative in some high areas of the province of Buenos Aires but not in the key producing regions.</p>
<p>&quot;In the producing regions the lowest temperature which was registered was four degrees C,&quot; Custodio said. &quot;If there were any frosts, they were very isolated.&quot;</p>
<p>((--Joelle Diderich, Sao Paulo newsroom +55 11 248 5417))</p>
